{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "moves.identifiers",
    "description": "Template library: the arithmetic that MOVES/NONROAD performs ON its identifiers, as opposed to the identifiers themselves. `polProcessID` is a packed pair, and every SCC fallback ladder is a decimal truncation, so both are arithmetic — not lookup tables, and not values to be written out by hand at each of the two dozen sites that need them. `null_output_column` is the one member that is not arithmetic on an identifier but the ABSENCE of one: MOVESOutput leaves nine of its twenty-five columns NULL on a NONROAD run -- zoneID, linkID, sourceTypeID, regClassID, fuelSubTypeID, engTechID, sectorID, hpID -- and a document that emitted 0 for them would be claiming zone zero rather than no zone. NaN is how a numeric column says absent, and the comparator reads NaN, NULL and empty as the same thing. `pol_process_id` packs the pair; `pollutant_id_of` and `process_id_of` unpack it, which the output stage needs because MOVESOutput carries the two halves in separate columns (nonroad_loader.rs:2183, :2371) -- and because a port that wrote `polProcessID / 100` at the output and `pollutantID * 100 + processID` at the input would have two chances to disagree with itself. The symbolic NAMES for identifier values live in each consuming component's `enums` block, because esm-spec §9.3 makes an `enums` block file-local and does NOT merge it across an `expression_template_imports` edge (see docs/esm-conventions.md §6, finding F3): a library that spelled `enum(\"pollutant\", \"NOx\")` in a body would fail to load in the importer with `unknown_enum`. Templates therefore take identifier VALUES as parameters, and the call site supplies them as `enum` ops.\n\nPRECISION. These templates carry the precision of the identifier bound to them, and that matters once a document declares `domain.element_type: \"Float32\"` (esm-spec 11.3.1, docs/esm-conventions.md 17). A ten-digit SCC is 135x binary32's exact-integer limit of 2^24, so a key-valued variable declares `element_type: \"Float64\"` and every expression over it -- `scc_zero_tail`'s `floor(scc/k)*k` included -- is then evaluated in binary64, which is what the Fortran's `INTEGER SCC` does. Two consequences for a call site. `tail_scale` is a LITERAL at every call site rather than a variable, because a literal adopts its context's precision while a `Float32` variable there would make the multiply a `mixed_element_type` error. And an identifier must reach a quantity through a COMPARISON, never through arithmetic: an equality inside a `join.on`, or an `ifelse` whose condition is one, hands the parent an exact 0/1 flag, whereas `flag*scc + (1-flag)*sccZero` puts a `Float64` key and a `Float32` flag under one `*` and does not compile. `null_output_column`'s `0.0/0.0` is precision-free -- NaN in both.\n\n`output_column_is_absent` is `null_output_column`'s inverse and exists because the absence it produces would otherwise be the one property of an output column that no inline assertion can pin: `expected` is a JSON number (esm-schema.json, `Assertion.expected`), so NaN cannot be written down, and every tolerance form is a magnitude comparison that a NaN actual fails -- measured, `actual=NaN expected=0` reports FAIL, which is the right verdict and the wrong polarity for a test that should pass. The way out uses only ops the format already has: IEEE says both `x > 0` and `x <= 0` are FALSE for a NaN, so `1 - [x>0] - [x<=0]` is 1 for an absent column and 0 for every real number, positive or negative. Measured on a three-row probe: 1 for 0/0, 0 for 4.25, 0 for -1.5. So a component can assert absence with a non-zero expected value, and the nine NULL columns of a MOVESOutput row stop being checkable only by the comparator.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "moves",
      "nonroad",
      "identifiers",
      "template-library"
    ]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "pol_process_id": {
      "params": [
        "pollutant_id",
        "process_id"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              100,
              "pollutant_id"
            ]
          },
          "process_id"
        ]
      }
    },
    "pollutant_id_of": {
      "params": [
        "pol_process_id"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "floor",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              "pol_process_id",
              100
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "process_id_of": {
      "params": [
        "pol_process_id"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
          "pol_process_id",
          {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              100,
              {
                "op": "apply_expression_template",
                "args": [],
                "name": "pollutant_id_of",
                "bindings": {
                  "pol_process_id": "pol_process_id"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "null_output_column": {
      "params": [],
      "body": {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
          0.0,
          0.0
        ]
      }
    },
    "output_column_is_absent": {
      "params": [
        "column"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
              1.0,
              {
                "op": "ifelse",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": ">",
                    "args": [
                      "column",
                      0.0
                    ]
                  },
                  1.0,
                  0.0
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "<=",
                "args": [
                  "column",
                  0.0
                ]
              },
              1.0,
              0.0
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "scc_zero_tail": {
      "params": [
        "scc",
        "tail_scale"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "floor",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "/",
                "args": [
                  "scc",
                  "tail_scale"
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "tail_scale"
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
